# Tigris SDK Patterns

Package: `@tigrisdata/storage` — install with `npm install @tigrisdata/storage`

## Environment Variables

The SDK reads credentials and bucket from these env vars automatically:

```bash
TIGRIS_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=tid_...
TIGRIS_STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=tsec_...
TIGRIS_STORAGE_BUCKET=my-bucket
```

- Never commit credentials to source control.
- Use `.env.local` or secrets management for keys.
- Tigris keys always start with `tid_` (access) and `tsec_` (secret).
- The bucket defaults to `TIGRIS_STORAGE_BUCKET` but can be overridden per-call via the `config` option.

## Core Functions

All functions return `{ data, error }`. Always check `error` first.

### `put` — Upload

```typescript
import { put } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await put("images/photo.png", file, {
  access: "public",        // "public" | "private"
  addRandomSuffix: false,  // append random chars to path (default: false)
  allowOverwrite: true,    // overwrite existing (default: true)
  contentType: "image/png",
  contentDisposition: "inline", // "inline" | "attachment"
  multipart: true,         // chunked upload for large files
  onUploadProgress: ({ loaded, total, percentage }) => {
    console.log(`${percentage}%`);
  },
});
// data: { path, url, size, contentType, contentDisposition, modified }
```

### `get` — Download

```typescript
import { get } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await get("images/photo.png", "file", {
  contentDisposition: "inline", // "inline" | "attachment"
});
// format: "string" | "file" | "stream"
```

### `head` — Object Metadata

```typescript
import { head } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await head("images/photo.png");
// data: { path, url, size, contentType, contentDisposition, modified }
```

### `remove` — Delete

```typescript
import { remove } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await remove("images/photo.png");
```

### `getPresignedUrl` — Presigned URL

```typescript
import { getPresignedUrl } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await getPresignedUrl("images/photo.png", {
  operation: "get",   // "get" | "put"
  expiresIn: 3600,    // seconds (default: 3600)
});
// data: { url, method, expiresIn }
```

### `list` — List Objects

```typescript
import { list } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

const { data, error } = await list({
  prefix: "images/",
  limit: 100,
  delimiter: "/",
});
// data: { items, paginationToken, hasMore }
```

## Error Handling

Always check `error` before accessing `data`:

```typescript
const { data, error } = await put("key", file);
if (error) {
  console.error("Upload failed:", error.message);
  return;
}
// Safe to use data
console.log(data.url);
```

## Pagination

Use `hasMore` + `paginationToken`:

```typescript
let token: string | undefined;
do {
  const { data, error } = await list({
    prefix: "uploads/",
    paginationToken: token,
  });
  if (error) break;
  for (const item of data.items) {
    // process item
  }
  token = data.hasMore ? data.paginationToken : undefined;
} while (token);
```

## Client Uploads

Client uploads use presigned URLs so files go directly from the browser to Tigris, bypassing your server.

```typescript
// Client — browser
import { upload } from "@tigrisdata/storage/client";

const result = await upload("my-file.png", file, {
  url: "/api/upload",    // your server endpoint (required)
  access: "private",
  multipart: true,
  partSize: 10 * 1024 * 1024,  // 10 MiB chunks
  concurrency: 4,               // parallel part uploads
  onUploadProgress: ({ loaded, total, percentage }) => {
    console.log(`${percentage}%`);
  },
});
// result: { url, name, size, contentType, contentDisposition, modified }
```

```typescript
// Server — API route (Next.js example)
import { handleClientUpload } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const body = await request.json();
  const { data, error } = await handleClientUpload(body);
  if (error) {
    return Response.json({ error: error.message }, { status: 500 });
  }
  return Response.json({ data });
}
```

### React Uploader Component

```typescript
import { Uploader } from "@tigrisdata/react";
import "@tigrisdata/react/styles.css";

<Uploader
  accept="image/*"
  multiple={true}
  multipart={true}
  concurrency={3}
  url="/api/upload"
  onUploadComplete={(file, response) => console.log(response.url)}
  onUploadError={(file, error) => console.error(error.message)}
/>
```

## Bucket Operations

```typescript
import { createBucket, getBucketInfo, listBuckets, removeBucket } from "@tigrisdata/storage";

await createBucket("my-bucket", { enableSnapshot: true });
await getBucketInfo("my-bucket");
await listBuckets();
await removeBucket("my-bucket", { force: true });
```

## Per-Call Config Override

Any function accepts a `config` option to override env vars for that call:

```typescript
await put("key", data, {
  config: {
    bucket: "other-bucket",
    accessKeyId: "tid_...",
    secretAccessKey: "tsec_...",
  },
});
```

